This product includes knowledge derived from the mruby project. The RITE
binary format, opcode definitions, argument specifications, and bytecode
semantics implemented by this project follow mruby 4.0.0.

The VM library consumes the bytecode package from go-mrbc and links the
regexp2 engine:

- go-mrbc (MIT), Copyright (c) 2026 go-mrbc contributors
- dlclark/regexp2 v1.11.5 (MIT), Copyright (c) Doug Clark

The gomruby command can also link the compiler stack:

- go-ruby-prism v1.3.0 (MIT), Copyright (c) 2024 Daniel Gatis
- Prism (MIT), Copyright 2022-present, Ruby developers; embedded as
  prism.wasm inside go-ruby-prism
- wazero v1.9.0 (Apache-2.0), Copyright 2020-2023 wazero authors

mruby is used as the bytecode and VM reference, not linked into the VM.
ChibiRuby is referenced as prior art; no code is copied.

